                                                "sense_id": "e77dd7c3-6ba2-376d-878f-accc64de02a6",
                                                "text": "1559-1566, John Knox, History of the Reformation in Scotland\n[A prince] is nothing but a servant, overseer, or grieve, and not the head, which is a title belonging only to Christ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b61c2717-6a89-477c-bfbd-eea6ecbe66c8",
                                                "sense_id": "e77dd7c3-6ba2-376d-878f-accc64de02a6",
                                                "text": "[T]heir children were horsewhipped by the grieve when found trespassing; […]"
